From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:49:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] Round 3: Gather the Moran update by target state

Store Moran transitions by target, with incoming entries in ascending
source order and then the source's parent/death order, and compute each
next probability as one sum instead of zeroing the next law and
scattering every source. Each target's floating-point additions keep
their order; zero-mass sources add +0.0. One logical step per state row
per update is still charged. A unit test compares the gathered law with
the scatter update bit for bit.

Workload: domain (48 Moran cases, population 18, 65 updates, full
records), 11 samples.
Before median: 4.432 ms. After median: 3.394 ms. Speedup: 1.31x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
